{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "HOS",
  "chapter": 12,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "HOS.12.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.12.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ephraim feedeth on wind, and followeth after the east wind: he daily multiplieth lies and desolation; and they do make a covenant with the Assyrians, and oil is carried into Egypt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.12.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.12.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD hath also a controversy with Judah, and will punish Jacob according to his ways; according to his doings will he recompense him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.12.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.12.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He took his brother by the heel in the womb, and by his strength he had power with God:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.12.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.12.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, he had power over the angel, and prevailed: he wept, and made supplication to him: he found him ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Beth-el, and there he spoke with us;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.12.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.12.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Even the LORD God of hosts; the LORD ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " his memorial.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.12.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.12.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore turn thou to thy God: keep mercy and judgment, and wait on thy God continually.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.12.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.12.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a merchant, the balances of deceit ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in his hand: he loveth to oppress.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.12.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.12.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Ephraim said, Yet I have become rich, I have found for myself substance: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all my labors they shall find no iniquity in me that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sin.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.12.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.12.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD thy God from the land of Egypt will yet make thee to dwell in tabernacles, as in the days of the solemn feast.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.12.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.12.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have also spoken by the prophets, and I have multiplied visions, and used similitudes by the ministry of the prophets.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.12.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.12.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " iniquity ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Gilead? surely they are vanity: they sacrifice bullocks in Gilgal; yes, their altars ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as heaps in the furrows of the fields.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.12.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.12.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Jacob fled into the country of Syria, and Israel served for a wife, and for a wife he kept ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "sheep",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.12.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.12.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And by a prophet the LORD brought Israel out of Egypt, and by a prophet was he preserved.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.12.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.12.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ephraim provoked ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to anger most bitterly: therefore will he leave his blood upon him, and his reproach will his Lord return to him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
